            Lesson(id: "en-foundations-connections-connectors", title: "Connectors: although, however, so", goal: "Link ideas with contrast (although, however) and result (so, because).",
                intro: LessonIntro(explanation: [
                            "Contrast: although + clause (“Although it was late, we went out”) and however + comma (“It was late. However, we went out.”).",
                            "Result: so joins cause → effect (“It was late, so we took a taxi”). Reason: because joins effect → cause (“We took a taxi because it was late”).",
                            "Punctuation: however needs a full stop or semicolon before it; although and because live inside the clause."], examples: [
                            ExampleLine(text: "Although it was expensive, we bought it.", meaning: "Contrast first."),
                            ExampleLine(text: "We bought it. However, we regret it now.", meaning: "However starts a new sentence."),
